---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Content Disclaimer" description="Important limitations and disclaimers for Network Academy educational content.">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">Content Disclaimer</h1>
    <div class="prose prose-neutral mt-6 dark:prose-invert">
      <h2>Educational use only</h2>
      <p>All lessons, examples, labs and tools on Network Academy are provided for educational purposes. They are not intended as professional advice and should not be relied upon as a substitute for professional engineering consultation.</p>

      <h2>RouterOS syntax and versions</h2>
      <p>Content targets RouterOS v7 syntax. Command syntax, properties and behaviour may vary across RouterOS releases and hardware profiles. Always consult the official MikroTik RouterOS documentation for your specific version before implementing any configuration.</p>
      <p>Generated configurations are templates only. Test all configurations thoroughly in a lab environment before applying to production networks.</p>

      <h2>No warranty</h2>
      <p>Everything on this site is provided "as is" without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including but not limited to warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, or non-infringement. The content may be outdated, inaccurate or contain errors.</p>

      <h2>Network changes carry risk</h2>
      <p>Network configurations can cause service outages, data loss or security exposure. Changes must be reviewed and adapted to your specific environment, tested in a lab before deployment, and executed with a rollback plan available. Keep console or out-of-band management access available to recover from mistakes.</p>
      <p>You are solely responsible for understanding and mitigating the risks of any network change you make.</p>

      <h2>BGP and routing policy</h2>
      <p>Announcing routes to the internet or to other networks affects their routing and traffic. Only announce address space and autonomous system numbers you are authorized to use. Filter all BGP sessions to prevent route leaks and address space abuse. Unfiltered BGP can cause widespread network disruption.</p>

      <h2>Lab environments vs production</h2>
      <p>Labs and simulations in this course are simplified educational models. Real networks have failover, redundancy, monitoring, compliance requirements and edge cases not represented in training materials. Behaviour observed in a lab may differ from production behavior due to scale, hardware limits, timing, or interactions with other services.</p>

      <h2>No liability</h2>
      <p>To the fullest extent permitted by law, Network Academy, its authors and developers assume no liability for any loss, damage, disruption or other harm arising from use of this site, its content, or configurations generated by its tools. This includes but is not limited to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Loss of service or data</li>
        <li>Unauthorized access or security breaches</li>
        <li>Damage to equipment or networks</li>
        <li>Cost of repair or recovery</li>
        <li>Loss of revenue or business opportunity</li>
        <li>Indirect, incidental or consequential damages</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Third-party content and trademarks</h2>
      <p>MikroTik, RouterOS, Winbox, Wireshark, GNS3, Cisco and other product or company names are trademarks of their respective owners. Network Academy is independent and is not affiliated with, endorsed by or sponsored by these organizations.</p>

      <h2>More information</h2>
      <p>For questions or clarification about this disclaimer, see our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>, <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a> or <a href="/contact">Contact page</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
